      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>“[I’m Spending] Hanukkah in Santa Monica” by Tom Lehrer was first written at the request of Garrison Keillor for his radio show <tei:hi rend="italic">The American Radio Company</tei:hi> on which it was performed twice, in 1990 and 1992. The song was later released on the album, <tei:hi rend="italic">Bible &amp; Beyond</tei:hi> (Larry Milder, 1999). The first recording of Tom Lehrer singing his song can be heard on <tei:hi rend="italic">The Remains of Tom Lehrer</tei:hi> (Disc 3) (2000). In 2022, Tom Lehrer gave an enormous Ḥanukkah present to the world, dedicating his entire oeuvre to the Public Domain including this song.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_49029_notes"/>
